# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# data/ is ignored WHOLESALE. It holds hundreds of GB of imagery, indexes, model weights and run output that must never enter
# history, and a new sub-folder must not be sweepable by `git add -A`. Only the small curated files that are already tracked
# (eval results, detection evidence, .gitkeep placeholders) are allowed back in, one explicit line each, below. A new file
# in an allowed folder is ignored too: add a `!` line here, on purpose, to track it.
# Git cannot un-ignore a file inside an ignored folder, so each folder on the way is un-ignored and its contents ignored again.
# (Generated from `git ls-files data`; regenerate rather than hand-edit if the tracked set changes.)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/*
!data/datasets/
data/datasets/*
!data/datasets/.gitkeep
!data/detect_eval/
data/detect_eval/*
!data/detect_eval/domain_shift_proxy.json
!data/detect_eval/eval_results.json
!data/detect_eval/evaluator_selftest.json
